    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "We present the progress we made during the current year on the Ontology and the web-based Knowledgebase of Fractures and Faults. The ontology makes explicit specifications of fractures and faults, their deformation mechanisms, and their properties. The knowledgebase has the ontology as its skeleton and features concepts of fractures and faults, their formation mechanism, their geometry and distribution, and their petrophysical properties including their effect on fluid flow. Concepts in the knowledgebase are discussed and supplemented by closely related concepts, photos, figures, illustrations, equations, and references. Here, we will introduce the major category of concepts and their interrelationships are discussed in the Ontology section. Our knowledgebase follows the same structure as the ontology and we will introduce it with a focus on faults.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Zhong, Jian, Aydin, Atilla and McGinness, Deborah L. (2008). Ontology and Knowledgebase of Fractures and Faults. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/gb568yb5588",
